const hello = pkgs.stdenv.mkDerivation({
  pname: "hello",
  version: "2.12.2",
  src: pkgs.fetchurl({
    url: "mirror://gnu/hello/hello-2.12.2.tar.gz",
    hash: "sha256-WpqZbcKSzCTc9BHO6H6S9qrluNE72caBm0x6nc4IGKs=",
  }),
  meta: { license: pkgs.lib.licenses.gpl3Plus },
});

console.log(hello.drvPath);
It runs in a browser. TypeScript is supported in every modern browser. You can evaluate nixpkgs in your tab, and it will fetch the compiled modules from GitHub as it needs them.2
2There is probably some fun code golf trying to create output paths that you then subsequently boot with trynix without ever using Nix. 
